      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It is important that a cardiologist knows and recognizes the entity of takotsubo cardiomyopathy or apical ballooning, but remains aware that a subsequent similar episode is not necessarily a recurrence of this syndrome. Relapse may be caused by \"classical\" coronary atherosclerosis, as described in this case report."},
